cartridge "SPIN & SOLVE/RICHARD BAIN/1987"

' SPIN & SOLVE
' A ColecoVision game based on "Wheel of Fortune" by Richard Bain, Ahoy!
' March 1987 (COMAL 0.14 for the Commodore 64, flip side of the disk,
' ahoy1987-03b: WHEEL'OF'FORTUNE, the phrase file RAN.WHEEL and its editor
' EDIT'WHEEL'DATA; orig/). The TV show's name, look and branding are not
' used: only the credits page names the original listing.
' Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic), 2026, in Amy by
' Amy Bienvenu.
'
' The game (the original's rules, read from its tokenized COMAL program and
' the article on the disk): 1 to 3 players, four rounds, a hidden phrase on
' the board each round; the players take turns starting a round. On a turn:
' - SPIN: the ball rolls round a 20-box wheel (the original drew a roulette
'   wheel with a rolling ball). The boxes, in the original's order:
'   600 750 350 1000 250 400 800 BANKRUPT 300 700 950 650 450 BANKRUPT 900
'   550 200 850 500 LOSE A TURN. BANKRUPT loses this round's money and the
'   turn, LOSE A TURN the turn. A value: pick a consonant; each time it is
'   in the phrase pays the value; a consonant not in the phrase loses the
'   turn.
' - BUY A VOWEL: $250 from this round's money (not enough: the turn is
'   lost); a vowel not in the phrase loses the turn.
' - SOLVE: right banks the round's money, at least the $200 house minimum;
'   wrong loses the turn.
' After four rounds the player with the most money (a tie: chosen at random)
' plays the bonus round: 5 consonants and a vowel are shown, then solve for
' $10,000, no time limit.
'
' Liberties:
' - Joystick, no typing: letters are chosen on a picker board (A-Z, used
'   letters dimmed); a solve is spelled into the board's hidden cards one
'   letter at a time (right button takes the last letter back).
' - A used letter on the picker is refused with a buzz instead of costing
'   the turn (the original lost the turn: on a joystick that is an input
'   slip, and the dimmed letter shows it is used).
' - SPIN is refused when no hidden consonant is left, BUY A VOWEL when no
'   hidden vowel is left (the original let you waste the turn).
' - No host option (a player typing in phrases needs a keyboard): phrases
'   always come from the original's file, 44 of its 45 ("WHEEL OF FORTUNE",
'   the show's name, left out), none repeated within a game. The data
'   editor (EDIT'WHEEL'DATA) edits the disk file and has no cartridge part.
' - Players are PLAYER 1-3 (no names typed); at most 3 players.
' - The ball's spin: hold the button to wind it up, release to roll; a
'   random part is always added, so the box can't be aimed.
' - Money is 5-digit BCD per round and 6-digit BCD banked.
'
' Controls: stick up/down and a button choose on menus; on the picker the
' stick moves the frame and the left button picks; when solving the right
' button takes a letter back. Either controller.
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128; the
' frame loop protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI off after a
' wait, display off. Music first in the sound table; the title tune played
' once. `set sprite count` always given. Nothing flashes faster than 3 Hz.

